---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { DATA_YEAR } from '../lib/salary';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="SalaryByCity's privacy policy: what little we collect, how cookies and analytics (GA4) and advertising (Google AdSense) work here, and the choices and rights you have."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl py-10">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400">Effective date: January 1, {DATA_YEAR}</p>

    <p class="mt-6 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      SalaryByCity is built to need as little of your data as possible. You can read every page on
      this site without creating an account, entering an email address, or telling us anything about
      yourself. We do not sell, rent, or trade personal information, and we do not operate as a
      lead-generation service. This policy explains the limited data that is collected when you
      visit, why, and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Information we collect</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      <strong>We collect no directly identifying information.</strong> There are no user accounts,
      registration forms, or newsletters. If you email us via the contact page, we receive your
      email address and message, use them only to reply, and delete them when the conversation is
      resolved. Like virtually all websites, our hosting infrastructure records standard server logs
      — IP address, browser type, pages requested, and timestamps — used solely for security and
      performance monitoring, and retained briefly.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Analytics (Google Analytics 4)</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      We use Google Analytics 4 (GA4) to understand aggregate usage — which pages are read, roughly
      where visitors come from, and how the site performs. GA4 sets cookies and collects device and
      usage information as described in
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400" rel="noopener">Google's Privacy Policy</a>.
      We have IP anonymization enabled, we do not upload any user-provided data to it, and we use
      the reports only in aggregate. You can opt out with the
      <a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400" rel="noopener">Google Analytics opt-out browser add-on</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Advertising (Google AdSense) and cookies</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      This site is supported by display advertising served by Google AdSense. Google and its
      partners use advertising cookies — including, where applicable, personalized-advertising
      cookies — to serve ads based on your visits to this and other websites. You can control
      personalized advertising at
      <a href="https://adssettings.google.com" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400" rel="noopener">Google Ads Settings</a>,
      and learn how Google uses data from partner sites at
      <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400" rel="noopener">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>.
      Visitors in regions with consent requirements (such as the EEA and UK) are shown a consent
      dialog before any non-essential cookies are set. You can also block or delete cookies at any
      time in your browser settings; the site's content works fully without them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Your rights</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      Depending on where you live (including under GDPR and CCPA/CPRA), you may have rights to
      access, correct, or delete personal information and to opt out of the "sale" or "sharing" of
      it. Because we hold essentially no personal data, most requests are satisfied already — but we
      will honor any request we can act on. Contact us at
      <a href="mailto:privacy@salarybycity.com" class="text-blue-700 underline dark:text-blue-400">privacy@salarybycity.com</a>.
      We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13, and this site is not directed
      at them.
    </p>

    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed text-stone-700 dark:text-stone-300">
      If our practices change — for example, if we ever add a newsletter — we will update this page
      and its effective date before the change takes effect. Material changes will be noted
      prominently on the homepage.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
